message: "If you use these certificates, records or code, please cite them as below."
title: "Certificates and reproducibility code for 'Global Pseudo-True Representation Exchange in Under-Modelled Spectral Fitting'"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mei
    given-names: Jinghang
    affiliation: "School of Electrical and Computer Engineering, The University of Sydney"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-2901-3285"
version: "2026.09.28"
date-released: "2026-09-28"
repository-code: "https://github.com/surnamemei/pseudo-true-representation-exchange"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - model misspecification
  - pseudo-true parameter
  - sinusoidal parameter estimation
  - nonlinear least squares
  - interval arithmetic
  - computer-assisted proof
abstract: >-
  Directed-rounding interval certificates (mpmath.iv), an independent Arb/python-flint replay
  implementation, preregistered numerical validation data, a sealed first-order prediction of
  noisy branch selection with its one-shot validation, and SHA-256 manifests for a study of
  global pseudo-true representation exchange in fixed-order (under-modelled) least-squares
  spectral fitting.
